  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Hindustan Coca Cola Beverages Pvt. Ltd vs State Of Bihar & Anr on 11 January, 2017",
    "facts": "2. The petitioner has challenged the order dated 30th November, 2006 passed in G.O. Case No. 164 of 2006 (Tr. No. 1340 of 2009) whereby cognizance has been taken against the petitioner for offence under Section 16 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954. 3. The prosecution report reveals that sample of Thumps up manufactured by the petitioner was seized by the Food Inspector, Madhubani with specific mention of the batch number. The seized article was sent for chemical analysis at the Combined Patna High Court Cr.Misc. No.49564 of 2013 dt.11-01-2017 Food and Drug Laboratory, Agamkuan, Patna-7. The only defect noticed was that date of manufacturing was not clearly visible on the sample.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the report of the analyst would reveal that there was no deviation of the Acts & Rules because if the same was not readable to the concerned analyst, it cannot be said that the date of manufacturing was not mentioned. He submits that, in similar circumstances, this Court had [LEAKAGE_MASK] the criminal prosecution in M/S Nestle India Limited vs. The State of Bihar & Ors. in Cr. Misc. No. 13737 of 2011 by order dated 05.08.201. 5. Learned counsel for opposite party no. 2 submits that prosecution report as well as report of the analyst would reveal that there is apparent violation of Rule 32 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1955. 6. In M/S Nestle India Limited case, the batch number as well as manufacturing date was not very clear to the public analyst.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the report of the analyst would reveal that there was no deviation of the Acts & Rules because if the same was not readable to the concerned analyst, it cannot be said that the date of manufacturing was not mentioned. He submits that, in similar circumstances, this Court had [LEAKAGE_MASK] the criminal prosecution in M/S Nestle India Limited vs. The State of Bihar & Ors. in Cr. Misc. No. 13737 of 2011 by order dated 05.08.201. 5. Learned counsel for opposite party no. 2 submits that prosecution report as well as report of the analyst would reveal that there is apparent violation of Rule 32 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1955. 6. In M/S Nestle India Limited case, the batch number as well as manufacturing date was not very clear to the public analyst.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
